<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kopperunchinga I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1216–<a href="/years/1242">1242</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kopperunchinga I was a chief of the Kadava family who ruled in the northern Tamil country in the early 13th century, as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Chola</a> power declined. Around 1231 he captured the Chola king Rajaraja III and held him at Sendamangalam, until the intervention of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoysala-empire">Hoysala</a> king Narasimha II forced his release.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kopperunchinga-i.jpg" alt="Kopperunchinga I" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Arimakhan · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kopperunchinga_I.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
